-- title:
--   Identity on the second component of the X₁(Mp) special fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a non-zero level $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $\{p\}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ obtained as `laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`, i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$; let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal, $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly; let $j \in K$, $j \neq 0$, have Laurent expansion the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) under `coeffEmb L`, and write $X =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChartModel A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L229) with its proper structure morphism `modelTo` to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$, glued from the finite chart $\mathrm{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin A K j` (the elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$) along `ιFin`. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$, and $X_k$ the pullback of `modelTo` along $\mathrm{Spec}\,k \to \mathrm{Spec}\,A$. Let $c_1 : C_1 \to \mathrm{Spec}\,k$ and $c_2 : C_2 \to \mathrm{Spec}\,k$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, and $i_1, i_2$ closed immersions of $C_1, C_2$ into $X_k$ over $k$ whose images cover $X_k$, with $C_1 \times_{X_k} C_2$ reduced of cardinality $n > 0$; let $\varepsilon$ be a section of `modelTo`, and $\varepsilon_1, \varepsilon_2$ sections of $c_1, c_2$ with $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ the base change of $\varepsilon$ to $k$. Further data, summarised here in groups: a semiring action of $L \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}} L$ on $A$ compatible with $A \to L$ and trivial after reduction to $k$; an integral weight-one form $w$ of level $M$ over $k$ together with a curve model $\mathrm{Mdl}_1$ of the Igusa function field `igusaFunctionFieldX1C k M w` and an isomorphism $e_1 : \mathrm{Mdl}_1.C \cong C_1$ over $k$, subject to the Gauss reading condition that every $a \in$ `chartAlgFin A K j` with $a \cdot y = x$ for power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $\bar y \neq 0$ pulls back along $e_1$, $i_1$ and the first projection to the function $\bar x / \bar y$ in Laurent series over $k$; arithmetic data $s \in L \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}} L$ and $b \in (\mathbb{Z}/p)^{\times}$ with $s\zeta = \zeta^{b}$, an integer $d$ coprime to $Mp$ with $d \equiv 1 \pmod M$ and $d \equiv b \pmod p$, an $L$-automorphism $\theta$ of $K$ inducing the base change of the diamond automorphism $\langle d \rangle$, an automorphism $w_d$ of $X$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ and an endomorphism $w_s$ of $X$ over $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the action of $s$ on $A$, both compatible through `ιFin` with ring automorphisms $\rho_d$, $\rho_s$ of `chartAlgFin A K j` realising $\theta$ and coefficientwise $s$; and an automorphism $u_k$ of $X_k$ over $k$ whose first projection is the first projection followed by $w_d$ and then $w_s$. Finally let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$, let $W_0$ be the valuation subring of $K$ consisting of those $f$ with $f \cdot y = x$ for power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $\bar y \neq 0$, and let $\mathfrak{P}_0 \neq \mathfrak{P}_1$ be minimal primes of $\varpi \cdot$ `chartAlgFin A K j` with $\mathfrak{P}_0$ the contraction of the non-units of $W_0$. If $\rho_d(\rho_s(g)) - g \in \mathfrak{P}_1$ for every $g$ in the chart algebra, then $i_2$ followed by $u_k$ equals $i_2$; that is, $u_k$ restricts to the identity on $C_2$.
--
--   This is the scheme-theoretic core of the assertion that an automorphism of the geometric special fibre of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ which is congruent to the identity on the finite chart modulo the minimal prime other than the centre of the Gauss valuation acts trivially on the corresponding component; the proof proceeds through the generic point of $C_2$ and separatedness of the fibre. It is used by [`ModularCurve.XOneP.comp_fibreIso_eq_of_diamondModelAut_galoisModelHom_of_gaussPin_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.comp_fibreIso_eq_of_diamondModelAut_galoisModelHom_of_gaussPin_twoChartModel_x1_mul), where the chart-level congruence is supplied by the interplay of an inertia twist with a diamond operator on the Igusa component.
